{"id":"word:hebrew:H335","type":"word","title":"אַי","subtitle":"H335 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"where? hence how?","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַי (H335) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 38 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַי (ʼay) means where? hence how? First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 13 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַי","transliteration":"ʼay","pronunciation":"ah'ee","strong":"H335","lemmaId":"hebrew:H335","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["אֵי","אֵֽי","אֵ֣י","אֵ֥י","וְ/אֵ֥י"],"morphs":[["HTi",26],["HC/Ti",6],["HTi/Sp3ms",2],["HTi/Sp3mp",2],["HTi/Sp2ms",1],["HC/Ti/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"where? hence how?","usage":"how, what, whence, where, whether, which (way).","full":"H335. ay [ אַי ] (, in Syriac in compounds as how ? W SG 120-2 ; compare Assyrian aiu , who? what? ). 1. interrogative adverb where? a. so with suffix אַיֶּ֫כָּה [a verbal form, see Sta § 355 b. 3 ] Gen 3:9 ; אַיּוֺ Exod 2:20 , poetry where is he? = he is nowhere Job 14:10 ; 20:7 ( Jer 37:19 read Qr אַיֵּה ); אַיָּם Nahum 3:17 (in indirect question) and the place thereof is not known, אַיָּם where they are. Idiomatically, with the suffix anticipating the noun to which it refers (Ew § 309 c , compare Dr Sm. i. 21, 14 ) 2Kin 19:13 מֶלֶחחֲֿמָת אַיּוֺ where is he , the king of Hamath? (|| Isa 37:13 אַיֵּה ) 19:12 ; Micah 7:10 . When used alone, or with other adverbs (see below), it is contracted to אֵי Gen 4:9 ; Deut 32:37 ; 1Sam 26:16 ; Prov 31:4 Qr. (The more usual form is אַיֵּה .) b. strengthened by the enclitic זֶה (see זֶה , 4 אֵיזֶֿה 15 where, then ? (never of a person , except Est 7:5 (late), & only once 1Kin 22:24 [but see 2Chr 18:23 ] with a verb ) Isa 50:1 ; 66:1 (twice in verse); Jer 6:16 , in indirect question 1Sam 9:18 ; in the phrase ֗֗֗ הַדֶּרֶח אֵיזֶֿה where is the way (that) . . . ? 1Kin 13:12 ; 2Kin 3:8 ; 2Chr 18:23 ; Job 38:19 a. 24. 2 prefixed to other adverbs or pron ., אֵי imparts to them an interrogative force: thus a. אֵיזֶֿה which (of two or more)? only Eccl 2:3 ; 11:6 (late), in indirect question b. אֵימִֿזֶּה whence ? ( מִזֶּה = hence ; see below זֶה ) Gen 16:8 בָאתְ אֵימִֿזֶּה 1Sam 30:13 ; 2Sam 1:3 , 13 ; Job 2:2 ; in indirect question Judg 13:6 ; 1Sam 25:11 ; with substantive annexed 2Sam 15:2 אַתָּה עִיר אֵימִֿזֶּה literally whence , as regards city, art thou ? Jonah 1:8 . c. אֵילָֿזֹאת Jer 5:7 upon what ground ? ( ᵑ9 super quo? how ? With other adverbs, אֵי coalesces into one word, see אֵיפֹה אֵיכָכָה, אֵיכָה, .","rootNote":"perhaps from 370 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 13 12","keyReferences":["1Kgs 13 12","1Kgs 22 24","1Sam 9 18","1Sam 25 11","1Sam 26 16","1Sam 30 13","2Chr 18 23","2Kgs 3 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":38,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 13 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":13,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵֽי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 24","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"1Sam 9 18","book":"1Sam","chapter":9,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 11","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"1Sam 26 16","book":"1Sam","chapter":26,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵֽי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"1Sam 30 13","book":"1Sam","chapter":30,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אֵ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ti"},{"reference":"2Chr 18 23","book":"2Chr","chapter":18,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi"},{"reference":"2Kgs 3 8","book":"2Kgs","chapter":3,"